    {
      "_id": "ddfb8a9f9ba086d2",
      "name": "Lore Reference: The Cold Door",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>The Cold Door</h2><p>[ASK] An old iron service door behind the dusty terminal. The ledger lists it as <strong>permanently sealed</strong>. Its old rune opens it for <strong>one minute</strong> when the last trolley of the night passes: \"the usual time\". One minute. Not two.</p><p>[EARN] On the other side: a snowy mountain road above Bridgehollow, a short walk from the Eirwitch camp. The far end of the line belongs at the gorge beside the camp, where some frost never melts (revealed after T1 is done, or when Europa's frost and Mottle's bell receipt are put to him: Insight <strong>DC 13</strong>).</p><p>Quill keeps the door's anchor rune (Threshold + Bind) running; it is Fraying (wrong iron, Hunger trace). If T1 fails, the open minute drifts 1d6 x 5 minutes later.</p><p><strong>He knows:</strong> the schedule, the capsules, the Bridgehollow news, who carried Europa in, the frost. <strong>He does not know:</strong> the vessel, the records, or the method beyond \"line and bell\".</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
